ible reasons for fluctuations in the world market price of tea.","topics":["1-3-5-the-determination-of-equilibrium-market-prices","1-3-4-price-elasticity-of-supply"],"board":"aqa","groups":["microeconomics"],"keywords":["commodity prices","tea","price volatility","supply"],"qpPage":32,"msPage":8,"ctxPage":28,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p1-2022-jun-q5","p":45,"section":"A","questionNumber":"5","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Using the data in Extract D (Figure 3), calculate, in percentage terms, how much more expensive a basket of groceries at Waitrose was than at Lidl in April 2020. Give your answer as a percentage to two decimal places.","topics":["1-3-5-the-determination-of-equilibrium-market-prices"],"board":"aqa","groups":["microeconomics"],"keywords":["grocery prices","supermarkets","calculation"],"qpPage":5,"msPage":10,"ctxPage":4,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p1-2019-jun-q1","p":42,"section":"A","questionNumber":"1","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":2,"questionText":"Using the data in Extract A (Figure 1), calculate the percentage change in the price of construction sand between January 2014 and January 2018. Give your answer correct to one decimal place.","topics":["1-3-5-the-determination-of-equilibrium-market-prices"],"board":"aqa","groups":["microeconomics"],"keywords":["price change","sand","calculation","market price"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":5,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-p1-2019-jun-q2","p":42,"section":"A","questionNumber":"2","parentQuestion":null,"choiceGroup":null,"marks":4,"questionText":"Explain how the data in Extract A (Figures 1 and 2) show that expansion in the global sand market is leading to prices of construction sand rising in real terms.","topics":["1-3-5-the-determination-of-equilibrium-market-prices"],"board":"aqa","groups":["microeconomics"],"keywords":["real prices","market expansion","supply and demand"],"qpPage":3,"msPage":6,"ctxPage":2,"modelAnswer":null},{"id":"aqa-